   "text": "This SMILES is my best reading of the drawing. Two parts are uncertain: the length of the long alkyl chain at the bottom left, and several stereocentres.\n\n**Peptide, N-terminus to C-terminus (read from the drawing):**\n- The N-terminal residue is acetyl-Lys, with its side-chain amine acylated by the linker described below.\n- Next come the first penicillamine (Pen, the C(CH3)2\u2013S residue), Asn, Thr and 7-methyl-Trp.\n- Then Lys(Ac), a second Pen, and Tyr with its phenol oxygen alkylated as O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013NH2.\n- Then 2-naphthylalanine, a 4-aminotetrahydropyran-4-carboxylic acid residue, Lys(Ac), Asn, and 3-pyridylalanine.\n- The C-terminus is N-methylglycinamide.\n- The two Pen residues are joined by an S\u2013S bond, which closes the macrocycle.\n\n**Linker on the N-terminal Lys side chain:**\n- It runs through two repeats of \u2013C(=O)CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013O\u2013CH2CH2\u2013NH\u2013.\n- Then comes \u2013C(=O)CH2CH2\u2013CH(\u2013CH2\u2013C(=O)\u2013alkyl)\u2013C(=O)\u2013NH\u2013, a glutamate-type unit.\n- That unit's amide nitrogen is attached to CH(CH2COOH)CH2N\u207a(CH3)3.\n\n**Uncertainties:**\n- I could not count the alkyl chain after the ketone reliably, so I used 12 carbons including the ketone carbon's neighbours, i.e. C(=O) followed by a straight 12-carbon chain.\n- I assigned L configuration to most residues as a default. The wedges and hashes at the Pen alpha carbons and at the glutamate-type and carnitine-like centres were not clear enough to settle.\n\nSMILES: CC(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCNC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)COCCOCCNC(=O)CC[C@H](CC(=O)CCCCCCCCCCCC)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(=O)O)C[N+](C)(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H]1C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2c[nH]c3c(C)cccc23)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCNC(C)=O)C(=O)N[C@H](C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccc(OCCN)cc2)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccc3ccccc3c2)C(=O)NC2(CCOCC2)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCNC(C)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](CC(N)=O)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2cccnc2)C(=O)N(C)CC(N)=O)C(C)(C)SSC1(C)C"
